I wouldn't bother enhancing darts, they're pretty shoddy weapons.

Daggers are good because (a) they can be used effectively both hand to
hand as missiles and (b) there are a few good artifacts that use the
dagger slot and (c) they are extremely common. Magicbane is the best
artifact dagger, but serpent's tongue and the flame/ice mage ones (I
forget the names) are good too.

Short swords are pretty good to use- there are lots of them in the
mines and early dungeon so there's a fair chance of finding a nicely
enchanted one. As a tourist you can enhance it up to skilled or beyond,
I think. There is at least one artifact short sword in [s] as well
(luckblade).

Long swords are good if you can find them. Even though you can't
enhance them very far, there are plenty of good artifact longswords.

Much the same for silver sabres, which have the obvious advantage
against silver haters. They are hard to come by though, untilyou have a
pet capable of taking on the minetown (or dungeon town) watch.



